---
/**
 * Terms of Service.
 *
 * Text is carried over from the live page with one correction: section 5 used to
 * list "the evidence wall" among the places that accept submissions, and that
 * feature was retired on 2026-09-17 — the terms were describing a form that no
 * longer exists.
 *
 * Parity contract (npm run verify:pages): title, description, canonical, one h1.
 * The live page carries NO structured data, so this one must not add any.
 */
import System from "../../layouts/System.astro";
import { SITE, SITE_NAME } from "../../lib/schema";

const title = "Terms of Service";
const description =
  "Terms of Service for Hunter Alpha Hub, an independent OpenRouter model information site: scope, data accuracy, acceptable use, user submissions, ads and liability.";
const canonical = `${SITE}/terms`;
---
<System title={`${title} | ${SITE_NAME}`} description={description} canonical={canonical}>
  <p class="kicker">Legal</p>
  <h1 class="display">Terms of Service</h1>
  <p class="byline"><span>Last updated: September 17, 2026</span></p>

  <section>
    <h2>1. Acceptance of These Terms</h2>
    <p class="body">
      These Terms of Service govern your use of www.hunteralphahub.com (the “Site”). By accessing or using
      the Site you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, please do not use the Site.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>2. What This Site Is</h2>
    <p class="body">
      The Site is an independent information resource about AI models available on OpenRouter. We publish
      model directories, comparisons, pricing tools and explanatory articles.
    </p>
    <ul class="list">
      <li>
        We are <strong>not affiliated with, endorsed by, or acting on behalf of</strong> OpenRouter or any
        model provider mentioned on the Site.
      </li>
      <li>
        Model names, provider names and logos are trademarks of their respective owners and are used for
        identification and comparison purposes only.
      </li>
      <li>
        The Site does not offer model inference. We do not host, proxy or resell access to any AI model.
        Requests to providers are governed by those providers' own terms.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>3. Data Accuracy</h2>
    <p class="body">
      Factual fields such as pricing, context window and supported modalities are read from public provider
      catalogues and are labelled with the date they were verified. Providers change pricing, availability
      and limits at any time, and models — especially unreleased “stealth” models — can be repriced or
      withdrawn without notice.
    </p>
    <ul class="list">
      <li>Always confirm current pricing and limits with the provider before relying on them.</li>
      <li>Information is provided for general guidance, not as a guarantee of any specific result.</li>
      <li>
        Where the Site separates verified facts from community speculation, speculation is clearly labelled
        and should not be treated as fact.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>4. Acceptable Use</h2>
    <p class="body">You agree not to:</p>
    <ul class="list">
      <li>use the Site in violation of any applicable law or regulation;</li>
      <li>
        send automated requests at a volume that degrades the Site for others, or attempt to bypass rate
        limits or access controls;
      </li>
      <li>attempt to probe, scan or test the vulnerability of the Site or its infrastructure;</li>
      <li>
        republish substantial portions of the Site's original content as your own, or present it as an
        official source;
      </li>
      <li>misrepresent your identity when submitting content to the Site.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>5. Submissions and Community Content</h2>
    <p class="body">
      Some areas of the Site accept user submissions (for example the newsletter form). When you submit
      content:
    </p>
    <ul class="list">
      <li>you keep ownership of what you submit;</li>
      <li>
        you grant us a non-exclusive, worldwide, royalty-free licence to display, format and distribute that
        content on the Site;
      </li>
      <li>
        you confirm you have the right to post it and that it is not unlawful, defamatory or infringing;
      </li>
      <li>
        we may remove any submission at any time, including content that is spam, off-topic or misleading.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="body">Data you submit is handled as described in our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>6. Third-Party Links, Ads and Tracking</h2>
    <ul class="list">
      <li>
        The Site links out to providers and other third parties. We do not control those sites and are not
        responsible for their content, terms or practices.
      </li>
      <li>
        Some outbound links may carry tracking or referral parameters that let the destination identify
        traffic coming from the Site. We measure outbound clicks in aggregate.
      </li>
      <li>
        Advertising is served by third-party networks. Those networks may use cookies or similar
        technologies subject to their own policies.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>7. No Professional Advice</h2>
    <p class="body">
      Content on the Site — including comparisons, recommendations, cost estimates and sample code — is
      general information. It is not legal, financial, security or professional advice, and it is not a
      substitute for your own evaluation before you commit engineering effort or spend money.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>8. Intellectual Property</h2>
    <p class="body">
      The Site's original text, layout, code and tooling are owned by us and protected by applicable law.
      You may quote short excerpts with attribution and a link. Bulk copying, scraping for republication, or
      presenting our content as your own is not permitted. Third-party trademarks remain the property of
      their owners.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>9. Disclaimer of Warranties</h2>
    <p class="body">
      The Site is provided “as is” and “as available”, without warranties of any kind, express or implied,
      including merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose and non-infringement. We do not warrant
      that the Site will be uninterrupted, error-free, or that any information it contains is complete or
      current.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>10. Limitation of Liability</h2>
    <p class="body">
      To the maximum extent permitted by law, we are not liable for any indirect, incidental, special,
      consequential or punitive damages, or for lost profits, revenue, data or goodwill, arising from your
      use of the Site or your reliance on its content — including costs incurred from model pricing, rate
      limits or service availability that differ from what the Site describes.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>11. Changes to These Terms</h2>
    <p class="body">
      We may update these terms from time to time. Changes take effect when posted on this page and the
      “Last updated” date is revised. Continued use of the Site after a change means you accept the updated
      terms.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>12. Contact</h2>
    <p class="body">Questions about these terms:</p>
    <ul class="list">
      <li>Email: <a href="mailto:privacy@hunteralphahub.com">privacy@hunteralphahub.com</a></li>
      <li>Website: <a href="https://www.hunteralphahub.com">www.hunteralphahub.com</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <p class="hero-actions"><a class="btn ghost" href="/">← Back to Home</a></p>
</System>

<style>
  .body {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }
  .list {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }
  .list li {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }
</style>
